@orangebeachcityschools 6th graders have spent the past two mornings with @cityoforangebeach Coastal Resources Dept studying biodiversity in Wolf Bay and watershed issues within the Gulf Frontal Perdido watershed.

They had a really close encounter with a dolphin that was hunting, removed 200+ lbs of litter and marine debris from Wolf Bay’s shoreline, learned to calculate biodiversity within a habitat using Simpson’s Index of Diversity, and discussed ways to become better environmental stewards within our coastal community ???

